;; Configuration for the documentation site, read by the docs-engine
;; (https://github.com/jlt-commons/docs-engine).
;;
;; Build it locally with `jolt site:build`/`jolt site:serve`. This repo is
;; still private, so CI only builds it on-demand (workflow_dispatch) for
;; now -- see .github/workflows/site.yml. Publishing (push/pull_request
;; triggers, the PUBLISH_SITE repository variable, GitHub Pages) is a
;; separate step for once the repo goes public.
{;; :base-path is what makes this a project site rather than an org one.
 ;; The site will be served at https://b12n-oss.github.io/lambda-mvp-rst/,
 ;; so every URL the engine emits needs that prefix. Leave it out and the
 ;; pages still render, but each one loads the ORGANIZATION site's
 ;; stylesheet and every asset 404s. The workflow has a check for exactly
 ;; this.
 :base-path   "/lambda-mvp-rst"

 :title       "lambda-mvp-rst"
 :description "An AWS Lambda custom runtime in Jolt whose handler builds its JSON response with real Rust (serde_json) via jolt-diplomat's Diplomat-based FFI bridge, plus a jolt bench tool for reproducing a cold-vs-warm boot-time comparison against your own AWS account."}
